+# Robot Pilot Runbook (simulation → shadow → canary → rollout)
+
+This runbook describes the safe, staged process to pilot a new perception/planning/control model on physical robots using Aegis.
+
+Prerequisites
+- Aegis stack deployed to staging with Postgres-backed registry, long-shadow, accounting, and Prometheus.
+- Evidence S3 bucket created with Object Lock enabled.
+- Keycloak configured and registry auth enabled.
+- Edge nodes labeled and reachable (node-role.kubernetes.io/edge=true).
+- Simulation environment (Gazebo/Isaac) available and Tekton pipeline configured.
+
+Stages
+
+1) Development & registry
+- Train model locally or in cloud.
+- Register model and upload version:
+  aegisctl register my-robot-model
+  aegisctl upload my-robot-model v1 --artifact /path/to/model.onnx
+- Add model card and test metadata in registry.
+
+2) Simulation verification (HIL / DT)
+- Run Tekton pipeline to execute N simulation episodes:
+  - Trigger the gazebo pipeline via Tekton Trigger (or:
+    tkn pipeline start gazebo-sim-pipeline -p episode_name=pilot -p duration_s=60 -p evidence_bucket=<bucket>)
+- Collect evidence in S3: s3://<EVIDENCE_BUCKET>/simulations/...
+- Run long_dryrun locally:
+  DRYRUN_ITERATIONS=2000 DRYRUN_WORKERS=40 python services/agent/long_dryrun_runner.py
+- Ensure planner schema/hallucination failure <= acceptance threshold.
+
+3) Long‑shadow (observe-only on device)
+- Deploy model to edge in shadow mode (no actuation). Use long-shadow deployment or lightweight agent to forward predictions to Aegis:
+  ./ops/scripts/run_long_shadow_campaign.sh --days 30 --sample-rate 0.01
+- Monitor divergence metrics daily via long-shadow supervisor; collect evidence and request SME signoff when metrics acceptable.
+
+4) Pilot actuated canary (human-in-loop)
+- Prepare canary robot with manual-override and emergency-stop hardware.
+- Deploy model to a single robot with wrappers and transaction_manager active.
+- Operator supervises in-person or remote; run short missions with live telemetry.
+- If safe, extend to small fraction of fleet (progressive rollout).
+
+5) Promotion & fleet rollout
+- When SME signoff obtained and acceptance criteria met:
+  - Run Model Promotion gate via GH Action or aegisctl to annotate model and trigger fleet pipeline.
+  - Deploy via canary → 10% → 50% → 100% with monitoring windows at each step.
+  - Use policy_controller to automatically mitigate non-critical workloads if carbon budgets or error rates spike.
+
+6) Incident & MTTR drills
+- Rehearse MTTR: run services/agent/mttr_drill.py to verify rollback and emergency-stop integration.
+- Postmortem: attach evidence artifacts to s3://<EVIDENCE_BUCKET>/incidents/<id> and fill postmortem template (ops/runbooks/postmortem_template.md).
+
+Safety checks (must pass before actuated pilots)
+- Wrapper audit (services/agent/wrapper_audit_runner.py) passes with no critical failures.
+- Long_dryrun acceptance thresholds satisfied.
+- Emergency-stop hardware tested and effective.
+- Transaction manager rollback tested and MTTR within SLO.
+- SME signoff artifacts present in S3.
+
+Notes
+- Keep human in the loop for first several weeks.
+- Collect and sign evidence for each step.
+- Use small sample rates for long-shadow initially to limit operational load and cost.
+
